[{"id":"sr-predict-q1","itemId":"shift-register","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"This is lesson 4.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">shift4</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> at a rising edge, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> at the next, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> from two edges ago. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is 1 just before the edges that start cycles 0, 1, 3 and 6. <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> takes each of those at that edge, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code> takes it from <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> at the next, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code> is 1 in cycles 1, 2, 4 and 7, and 0 everywhere else.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"shift4-q1","source":"hdl/level-04/shift4/shift4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":10,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"shift4_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"shift4_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q[1]","path":"shift4_tb.q1","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"],[8,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","0","0","1","0","0"]}]},"answer":"q[1]","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"sr-predict-q3","itemId":"shift-register","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 4.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">shift4</code>: at each rising edge <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> and every other bit the one below it. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code>, the last bit, for every cycle. <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> was 0 at the three edges before cycle 0.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> from four edges ago: each edge moves the value up one place, through <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">q[1]</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">q[2]</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code>. So <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> in a cycle is the value <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> had just before the edge that started the cycle three earlier. <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is 1 at the edges that start cycles 0, 2, 3, 4, 7 and 9, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> is 1 in cycles 3, 5, 6, 7 and 10; the 1 from cycle 9 reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> after the window ends. In cycles 0 to 2, <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> shows the 0s from before the window.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"shift4-q3","source":"hdl/level-04/shift4/shift4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":12,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"shift4_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"],[9,"1"],[9.5,"0"],[10,"1"],[10.5,"0"],[11,"1"],[11.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"shift4_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8.5,"1"],[9.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q[3]","path":"shift4_tb.q3","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[8,"0"],[10,"1"],[11,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","0","1","0","1","1","1","0","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q[3]"},{"id":"sr-find-bug","itemId":"shift-register","role":"core","promptHtml":"This shift register should take <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> in at <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> and move every bit up one place at each rising edge, so that <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> from four edges ago. Its testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>In a concatenation the leftmost part goes at the top (lesson 4.3). <code>{d, q[3:1]}</code> puts <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> into <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> and moves every other bit down one place, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q[3]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> from one edge ago and <code class=\"nobreak\">q[0]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> from four. Written <code>{q[2:0], d}</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> goes in at the bottom and the bits move up.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-04/shift4_bug/shift4_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A 4-bit shift register. At each rising edge every bit moves up one","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// place and d comes in at the bottom, so q[0] is d one edge ago and q[3]","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// is d four edges ago.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"shift4_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"{","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"d, q[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"]","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"}","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":10,"fixLine":"q <= {q[2:0], d};"},{"id":"sr-fill-line","itemId":"shift-register","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">delay16</code> delays <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> by 16 cycles with a 16-bit shift register, <code class=\"nobreak\">line</code>, whose top bit is the output. At each rising edge, every bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">line</code> should move up one place and <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> should go in at the bottom. Type the right-hand side.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>{line[14:0], d}</code> joins the lower fifteen bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">line</code> with <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> into sixteen bits, the leftmost part at the top (lesson 4.3). So bit 15 takes bit 14, and so on down to bit 0, which takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>; after 16 edges, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">line[15]</code>. With <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> on the left, the bits would move down instead, and <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> would reach the output after one edge.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-04/delay16/delay16.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":14,"before":["// q is d delayed by 16 cycles of clk. line is a 16-bit shift register","// with no reset, and only its last bit leaves the module.","module delay16 (","  input  logic clk,","  input  logic d,","  output logic q",");","  logic [15:0] line;","","  always_ff @(posedge clk)"],"blankLine":{"left":"    line <= ","right":";"},"after":["","  assign q = line[15];","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// q is d delayed by 16 cycles of clk. line is a 16-bit shift register","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// with no reset, and only its last bit leaves the module.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"delay16","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"15","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] line;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    line ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" line[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"15","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["{line[14:0], d}"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The right-hand side"},{"id":"sr-report-srl","itemId":"shift-register","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built lesson 4.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">delay16</code>, a 16-bit shift register with no reset, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Slice Logic table of its Utilization report. Slice LUTs counts every LUT the design uses, and the rows indented under it say what each does: logic, or memory, which includes LUTs used as shift registers.","explanationHtml":"<p>One: the SRL16E that holds the middle of the line (lesson 4.3). LUT as Logic is 0, because nothing needs working out, and Slice Registers is 2, the flip-flops at the two ends of the line. <code class=\"nobreak\">delay16_rst</code>, the same line with a reset, uses no LUT at all and 16 Slice Registers, because an SRL16E cannot be reset.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/delay16/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":32,"excerpt":["+----------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","|          Site Type         | Used | Fixed | Prohibited | Available | Util% |","+----------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","| Slice LUTs                 |    1 |     0 |          0 |     63400 | <0.01 |","|   LUT as Logic             |    0 |     0 |          0 |     63400 |  0.00 |","|   LUT as Memory            |    1 |     0 |          0 |     19000 | <0.01 |","|     LUT as Distributed RAM |    0 |     0 |            |           |       |","|     LUT as Shift Register  |    1 |     0 |            |           |       |","| Slice Registers            |    2 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Flip Flop    |    2 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Latch        |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","| F7 Muxes                   |    0 |     0 |          0 |     31700 |  0.00 |","| F8 Muxes                   |    0 |     0 |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","| Unique Control Sets        |    1 |       |          0 |     15850 | <0.01 |","+----------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+"],"ask":"How many LUTs does delay16 use as shift registers?","answer":"1","numeric":true}]